{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/view/artifact-controller.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:32:59.729403Z","id":"7bec3684a53d4d228891f147137a443ef36e11d906cba05a2696681207c4cf0e","body":{"detail":"frameLoaded() closes the gate on a load with no hello, calls leaveDocument() (host.leave()), and asks the page to greet again with clax:greet. The page's hello reopens the gate, but the capability host starts over, so everything the page had set up through it ends and the page must set it up again. The spec states this as an open limitation (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-28-clax-design.md:1167-1171).","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":624},"end":{"line":642},"content_hash":"72305be614779699d14d6ef0e341ca8695bf7df61efd86ed49f766a51dfdd6f9"},"suggested_fix":"When the hello that answers clax:greet comes from the same document (same artifact, version and file), keep or re-establish the host's room joins, db subscriptions, sample streams and custom anchors instead of starting over.","summary":"Back or Forward across a page's own fragments drops its room joins, db subscriptions, sample streams and custom anchors","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/view/frame-host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:32:59.730281Z","id":"4d1b4269e54dea08437973adcfaa170940e1002bace91f85d9601704550dd67a","body":{"detail":"With the viewer's activation, a subdomain-mode page can navigate the top window to another site or a fresh Clax load (docs/contract.md, Known limitations). Every load starts with the keyboard trail tainted, so what remains is C and ? live in the fresh load, and the navigation itself. Giving this frame sandbox='allow-scripts allow-same-origin allow-forms allow-modals allow-popups allow-popups-to-escape-sandbox allow-downloads' (no top navigation) would stop a navigation to another site; it needs every capability and page link checked first, and a popup the page opens keeps the shell's live keys either way. Decision needed: sandbox the subdomain frame or not.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":61},"end":{"line":66},"content_hash":"431b45f7af17766e5236279b541ce64c1c05c8e23949fa4e3cd7257ec710cfa5"},"summary":"The subdomain-mode frame has no sandbox, so a page can navigate the whole window","tags":["status:needs-decision","security","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/view/trail.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:32:59.730318Z","id":"2ae15dfc4b730f67ed2966a0113bcaa47b3ecf806ab2b2d73e3ad65874f37bea","body":{"detail":"No key clears the tainted trail, and every load starts tainted, so keyboard-only and screen-reader viewers need a pointer for Send, Resolve, Reply, the batch sends, a page-opened composer's Post, and the prompt's Allow. A path a page cannot coax (for example: the control held focus for ALLOW_DELAY_MS with no other key in between) would restore keyboard use. Decision needed: add such a path or not.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":41},"end":{"line":50},"content_hash":"6f6b435ae268b57cdf1b57ffc3db1fed62b7b5ee97e1f5ee6deedc2734083c92"},"summary":"No keyboard path for consequential actions once the trail is tainted","tags":["status:needs-decision","security","a11y","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/view/deltas.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:32:59.731087Z","id":"3840a663992442d3b8d393dbb11a44ad1af9839c853aa64d6b44e0a1fa87264b","body":{"detail":"The artifact:<id> topic carries a thread's newest comment and its count; a view that missed a comment, or holds one deleted or edited before the newest, gets complete false and fetches that thread whole.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":13},"end":{"line":29},"content_hash":"dde23580758adb5c4ed4da369bdac4d1fbbfe066c2e5b056c20725d2c2610604"},"summary":"A thread delta whose comments do not add up fetches the thread whole","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/view/artifact-stream.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:32:59.731122Z","id":"93f0d25e0a13aee591cc4816b13d291787bc44c99eb625e669d011e2d9bbc274","body":{"detail":"A page's own publish (artifact.publish) moves every open unpinned view to the new version when the view hears its version event, which carries by_page (lines 115-128). A view whose stream goes live only after that publish learns of the version from this refetch on ready, which cannot tell who published, and offers Reload in the top bar. The browser tests wait for each view's stream before a vote (streamLive in web/e2e/fixtures.ts:203).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":148},"end":{"line":153},"content_hash":"a91a85289e6e1f0f950c25198984f37c048a7650c830e9460e903fe262484c32"},"summary":"A view that missed a page's publish offers Reload rather than following it","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/view/artifact-controller.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:32:59.731329Z","id":"76a00f1b49d5b22fa1e7deb61eece0b7ae52086b335bcdb05f2bc760a5b46906","body":{"detail":"After clax:degraded, the shell holds the part failed for that page: Comment stays off and says so, even once the bridge's own retry could load the part, and threads whose anchors went unanswered while it failed stay unplaced. This needs a protocol addition.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1233},"end":{"line":1243},"content_hash":"d916958d7195a5a877a49f0b9d1b6e048afccef5dc947da03e0bf784247f5cbe"},"suggested_fix":"Have the bridge report a part that loads after failing; the shell then clears failedParts for it and its notice, and resolves the anchors again.","summary":"A lazy part that failed stays failed until the page's next hello, even once it loads","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/view/viewer-name-model.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:26:52.183434Z","id":"96f44240940c1fa64105e9efc9072f147bf9e458a719255159c9bd5c73d8299f","body":{"detail":"save() runs for the Enter that saves the name and again for the Escape or blur that follows. Both pass the `next === this.saved` check before the first request answers (this.saved is set only in its .then), so the daemon receives the same rename twice and threads.ts announces the viewer twice. The stream hub ignores the repeated reconnect (web/shell/src/stream-hub.ts, `reconnect` case), so the cost is one extra request and one extra announcement per rename.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":39},"end":{"line":47},"content_hash":"85e6dd8736724daec080d4f5e58dedddeb783098b0c4af3e77df622a1f99526f"},"suggested_fix":"Remember the name whose request is in flight and skip a save of the same name until it answers.","summary":"A rename can send two identical PUT /api/viewers/me requests","tags":["review","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/view/artifact-stream.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:38:28.460502Z","id":"69abb375e48b9757b02124e6d05bf820e28c661a3a33cc98d15d34112f5cfbd5","body":{"detail":"A page's own publish (artifact.publish) moves every open unpinned view to the new version when the view hears its version event, which carries by_page (lines 115-128). A view whose stream goes live only after that publish learns of the version from this refetch on ready, which cannot tell who published, and offers Reload in the top bar. The browser tests wait for each view's stream before a vote (streamLive in web/e2e/fixtures.ts:203).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":163},"end":{"line":168},"content_hash":"a91a85289e6e1f0f950c25198984f37c048a7650c830e9460e903fe262484c32"},"summary":"A view that missed a page's publish offers Reload rather than following it","supersedes":"93f0d25e0a13aee591cc4816b13d291787bc44c99eb625e669d011e2d9bbc274","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/view/whole-comment.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T19:00:38.378205Z","id":"bae1381fece00ecd9a12fcca5e56ffd7e8ccec9e4948bb1b2f0e14cfe6187725","body":{"detail":"create() repeats threads.ts createThread (the multipart POST to /api/artifacts/<aid>/threads) for the one anchor it sends, because importing createThread from this lazy chunk adds an export to the artifact entry, which is at its gzip budget (web/perf/bundle-budget.json artifact: 63988). A change to the create route's fields or error shape must be made in both.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":23},"end":{"line":36},"content_hash":"2a984369e8dbe835290769802543595196115f39d8db6884206a2eef93117dd1"},"suggested_fix":"Import createThread from ../threads once the entry has slack under its budget.","summary":"postWhole posts with its own copy of createThread","tags":["revisit:the artifact entry has slack under its bundle budget","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/view/whole-comment.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T19:10:14.562459Z","id":"b0a5932189ef2f713cfb216da2bae00f94bc00d4eff4d51b690ce3272bdf9a95","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:ffd6520","summary":"postWhole now posts with threads.ts createThread; the local create() copy is gone. Evidence: `npx vitest run shell/src/new-comment.test.ts` passes, including the post's multipart fields (anchor, version, body, no clip) and the failure notice.","supersedes":"bae1381fece00ecd9a12fcca5e56ffd7e8ccec9e4948bb1b2f0e14cfe6187725","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/view/send-target.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:22:22.163118Z","id":"2dcd9e9a1ff7a7741cbc1590b739ee7dd70f018ac4d83bf86d885355bc5562fb","body":{"detail":"Failure: with the owner's agents idle and Sam's agent the most recently active live agent on the artifact, every one of the owner's thread cards reads 'Send to sam-notes' and the unsent bar 'Send 2 unsent to sam-notes': one press routes the owner's thread to Sam's agent and makes routing requests for every author Sam has not approved. Sam's browser likewise defaults to the owner's 'codex'. defaultTarget takes the first live agent in the daemon's order (most recently active) whatever its person; the label (web/shell/src/ui/Sidebar.svelte:137, the SendButton labels) shows the name alone, and 'Sam approves first' only inside the menu. Spec 2026-10-08 section 10 lists 'Your agents' first, and section 11 'Display' shows an agent's person wherever more than one person's agents appear. Seen in Chromium at 1280 and 390 px on a scratch daemon at commit f7a89d53.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":14},"end":{"line":20},"content_hash":"ef68ead27c64939ff056da5af4ff407035ba481532b538dfc1b9243ee69001c3"},"suggested_fix":"Default to this viewer's own most recent live agent (its person's public ID equals the viewer's; the owner's for the owner), else none (an untargeted send); keep another person's agent only when this viewer chose it. When the target is another person's agent, say so on the button ('Send to sam-notes (Sam's)') and carry 'Sam approves first' there too. Add a unit test for defaultTarget with another person's agent listed first.","summary":"The default Send target can be another person's agent, and the Send button names it without its person","tags":["review","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/view/working-model.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:22:22.163856Z","id":"80b94326fd39bd9aa341d7fba9df359e9050c7e3932db3c00a298a973290872d","body":{"detail":"With the owner's and Sam's agents on one artifact the top bar reads '4 open threads · codex, claude-2, sam-notes idle' with no person, and the question card of an agent named 'clax-multi-person-agent-strip-ab' reads 'claude in tmp' with the button 'Answer claude', while the inbox strip above names the same agent 'clax-multi-person-agent-strip-ab'. Spec 2026-10-08 section 11 'Display' shows agents by name, with their person wherever more than one person's agents appear.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":37},"end":{"line":45},"content_hash":"77ba540b5356c9ce6515c878d43d20a54dbca0f2a96f33a9728bcd7450ed90eb"},"summary":"The artifact view's summary line and question cards name agents without their person, or by harness","tags":["review","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/view/send-target.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:49:36.255908Z","id":"4952e1338ecf624ed58f12966f5d0faf4f6567492f3a09764484e16c69e3632f","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:bb547990","summary":"defaultTarget keeps only the viewer's choice; with none, ShellSidebar sends to the viewer's own most recent live agent (ownTarget, web/shell/src/view/send-menu.ts), and with only other people's agents live the Send button opens the menu (no one-press send). Labels naming another person's agent name the person ('Send to sam-notes (Sam's)'), as do menu entries ('Sam's agent'). Evidence: send-target.test.ts ownTarget tests (Sam's agent listed first: the owner's own is chosen; none for only others' agents or an unknown viewer), send-menu.test.ts and thread-owner.test.ts 'the Send target' tests, and web/e2e/agent-strip.spec.ts pass.","supersedes":"2dcd9e9a1ff7a7741cbc1590b739ee7dd70f018ac4d83bf86d885355bc5562fb","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/view/working-model.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:49:36.258457Z","id":"baf1e6ed51f2ee285bc15494768f5dee627fecf5d208b1cdef98ac579055d7eb","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:bb547990","summary":"The top bar names another person's agents with their person where more than one person's agents appear ('sam-notes (Sam's), codex, claude idle'; withPeople in web/shell/src/view/agent-display.ts), and question cards and inbox items name an agent by its name (question and inbox views carry the agent's name; agentLabel uses it). Evidence: agent-display.test.ts and q/model.test.ts pass; target/t22/shots-r1/owner-chose-sams-agent-1280-light.png shows the summary.","supersedes":"80b94326fd39bd9aa341d7fba9df359e9050c7e3932db3c00a298a973290872d","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/view/artifact-stream.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T03:39:10.582430Z","id":"f24d4a1da7f7eb403fab46dcd276840221f49de288e4fdba253b654760c5ef65","body":{"detail":"Failure: a view opened without boot data (ArtifactController.start calls loadThreads, then the stream opens) whose stream 'ready' precedes the threads answer. A feedback_state for an existing thread T arrives while v.threads() lacks T, so it is kept in `early` (line 101). The load then brings T without a `thread` event, so the entry is never taken or dropped; later feedback_state events for T apply directly. At T's next `thread` event (any reply), lines 108-111 put the old early state on it, replacing the newer one, and the card shows a stale delivery label until the next state change. Reproduced with a vitest probe in the harness of web/shell/src/view/artifact-stream.test.ts: ready; feedback_state since 1 for t1 (not held); threads set to t1 with since 2; feedback_state since 3; delta('open', 2, 'c2') -> t1.feedback_state.since is '1', expected '3'. The window is narrow (the first load starts before the stream opens). `ready` and `resync` clear the buffer, so it is bounded and no stale state survives a resync.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":98},"end":{"line":111},"content_hash":"dfc053d7d20597096f315dfdce47fbdc8b36c392bb8dac13b1622208dccd22a3"},"suggested_fix":"Use an early state only when the thread event adds the thread (the view did not hold raw.id), and drop the entry either way.","summary":"A delivery state kept for a thread the first load then brings is applied over newer states at that thread's next thread event","tags":["review","people","spec:10","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/view/artifact-stream.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T03:49:52.923117Z","id":"03f068e233fa8762f2513d42afba4247113b5914794617dfd8c1bc7a6275b2df","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:7ed8fcc4","summary":"Fixed: ArtifactStream gives a kept early state only to a thread event that adds the thread, and a state applied to a held thread drops the kept one. artifact-stream.test.ts 'never applies a state kept early over a newer one once the first load brought its thread' (with and without a newer state heard) reproduces the probe (ready; state since 1 for an unheld t1; the load sets t1 since 2; state since 3; a reply's thread event) and passes, reading since 3 (or 2); without the adds-only guard both cases read since 1.","supersedes":"f24d4a1da7f7eb403fab46dcd276840221f49de288e4fdba253b654760c5ef65","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/view/send-menu.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T03:49:30.467921Z","id":"80c0e0f0cd273030480744a514e727c7965f3c2e93cfad438ff4a3333feb7c12","body":{"detail":"Failure: the extension panel with state.viewer null (the worker's GET /api/viewers/me failed while the artifact read succeeded, web/extension/src/sw/tabs.ts:751-760) and one live agent of the owner (person {owner: true}) shows 'Send to …' with no caret; pressing it sets the menu open, but SendButton renders the menu only when more than one agent is live or one is another person's (web/shell/src/ui/SendButton.svelte:29-34), so nothing opens and nothing is sent. Reproduced with a throwaway Panel unit test (viewer: null, one owner agent): buttons ['Send to …'], sent [], no menu, no caret. Before a3ae32de that Send went to the live agent. Panel.svelte:64-67 passes me?.public_id (undefined) to ownTarget, whose contract is 'with me unknown, no agent with a person is', while sendGroups (same file, lines 22-31) and SendButton take an unknown viewer as the owner. Elsewhere.svelte:90 has the same gap for other pages' cards.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":42},"end":{"line":49},"content_hash":"ccd7d6eaaa897ed090c036741db032a1b4e6c698b3ec5a69f13a83b6ede5b6c9"},"suggested_fix":"Make ownTarget take an unknown viewer as the owner, as sendGroups does (match person.owner when me is undefined), or have SendButton open the menu whenever target is null and agents are live.","summary":"With the viewer unknown, ownTarget names no agent while sendGroups calls the owner's agents yours: the panel's Send is then a dead button","tags":["review","task:23","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/view/send-menu.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T03:49:30.468094Z","id":"09641bfec1e971b5ad720b28eacc5865e3f086fee6c4979cf75adb2fcb20ab3f","body":{"detail":"Panel.svelte:69 assigns firstsVia.ask on each instantiation; the last Panel mounted wins and the assignment outlives it. Not a security boundary: module bindings are unreachable from a page, a content script or an artifact frame, and same-realm code could already replace fetch; the hook ignores `aid` and the worker derives the page from the threads (web/extension/src/sw/panel.ts:157-165), so the panel cannot aim it at another artifact. But it is hidden coupling between the shell's lazy SendMenu and one host.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":9},"end":{"line":14},"content_hash":"757b87c01cabe4d022e52d5252fbae54ae87cde78aec021e38be557e930bc699"},"suggested_fix":"Pass the asker down as a prop (Sidebar -> SendButton -> SendMenu) or through a Svelte context set by the host, with the fetch as the default.","summary":"firstsVia is a module-global hook a component sets as a side effect of its init and never resets","tags":["review","task:23","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/view/send-menu.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T04:05:29.986870Z","id":"2881e9d6d8c9a79d85c0ce25f33c267d1808a041a27f140c306d894b69ef3ee8","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:21d2a440","summary":"The panel and its other-page cards pass ownerOf(agents, me) to ownTarget (web/extension/src/panel/adapt.ts): the viewer's public ID, else the one the owner's agents carry, so Send goes to the owner's own agent while the viewer is unknown. Evidence: Panel.test 'sends to the owner's own agent while the daemon has not named the panel's viewer' passes. The shell's ownTarget rule is unchanged.","supersedes":"80c0e0f0cd273030480744a514e727c7965f3c2e93cfad438ff4a3333feb7c12","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/view/send-menu.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T04:05:29.988289Z","id":"42783922b8ba3f81fe267c68402d4af7730dcab7f89a8dc9e7312312cfa716d1","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:21d2a440","summary":"Panel.svelte sets firstsVia.ask in an $effect while mounted and clears it on unmount when it is still its own, so no panel's hook outlives it. Evidence: the Panel and Send-menu tests that ask through the worker pass (web units 1568/1568).","supersedes":"09641bfec1e971b5ad720b28eacc5865e3f086fee6c4979cf75adb2fcb20ab3f","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/view/send-menu.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T22:24:19.594140Z","id":"2abc0c544ce6da85d3a58fc62a3b8394a111e7c194a223b28dc411e9c8db3307","body":{"detail":"Failure: a single-owner install served with `clax serve --bind 0.0.0.0`, one live agent of the owner's (`web`); a LAN viewer comments on its page. The thread's button reads \"Send to …\" and the batch button \"Send 1 unsent to …\"; pressing either opens a menu headed \"The owner's agents\" instead of sending. On main the same viewer read \"Send to claude\" and one press sent (main's `defaultTarget` fell back to the most recent live agent). `ownTarget` takes only agents with no person or the viewer's own person, and every agent now carries `person` (the owner's agents too), so a viewer who is neither the owner nor a person never has a default. Spec 2026-10-08 §19 lists what changes for a single-owner install and does not list this; §10's \"with only other people's agents live there is none\" was written for connected people, while a LAN viewer's comments reach the owner's agents without approval (O6). Either keep the owner's most recent live agent as the default for a viewer who is not a connected person, or record the change as a §19 item.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":47},"end":{"line":49},"content_hash":"1d8478e287824c25299fd664666ca96b06c0a5c20821bd9994db56d6c725dbe5"},"suggested_fix":"In ownTarget, treat the owner's agents as the default for a viewer who is not a connected person (the shell knows `person` from /api/viewers/me), and test it in a single-owner e2e as a LAN viewer.","summary":"A LAN viewer of a single-owner install loses the one-press Send: every Send reads \"Send to …\" and opens a menu","tags":["review","final-review-ui","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/view/publisher.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T22:24:19.594350Z","id":"26259f1eb68709afb1695dd9f23fe8520b96f65b4c413d15706122e0c6c65229","body":{"detail":"On a single-owner install with one agent named `web`: the artifact header reads \"published by claude\" (publisher.ts:8, `owner_harness`), the gallery card \"claude · just now\", the inbox's Agent filter offers \"claude\" and \"claude 3d4f · web\" (q/InboxPage.svelte:105), and the roster tokens show \"cl\" for every Claude agent (ui/Roster.svelte:42-43): with four live agents the top bar shows cl cl cl cl, and their titles give the name without the person. Meanwhile Send, the strip, owner chips and inbox titles say `web`. Spec 2026-10-08 §19 item 1: names are \"shown where the shell showed the harness\".","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":8},"end":{"line":8},"content_hash":"8c93b4182a8a56604bdd85bff940aca6c017fd290124b55a1e5fb4131dc70844"},"summary":"Places that showed the harness still show it, where spec §19 item 1 says the agent's name now shows","tags":["review","final-review-ui","naming","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/view/send-menu.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T03:13:17.303713Z","id":"c37297f6f9ed6323cdd1c95b10c45bd68e4578b0644cf2aeb7ad6d9c4e38ed65","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"2abc0c544ce6da85d3a58fc62a3b8394a111e7c194a223b28dc411e9c8db3307","summary":"Coordinator ruling (2026-10-15): the one-press Send default for the owner and connected people stays their own newest live agent. A viewer who is neither (a LAN viewer) keeps single-owner behaviour: one press sends to the owner's newest live agent and the button names it (\"Send to claude\"); with only connected people's agents live, the menu opens. Spec §10 states it (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person-design.md, the one-press Send bullet).","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/view/send-menu.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T03:13:17.303855Z","id":"b8f33ddf9e78dfc5667db67b20cfa3c23f266c19c67e24ceb7ee02b81bc9561b","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:3724ee8f","summary":"A LAN viewer's Send takes the owner's agents as its own (sendsFor in web/shell/src/view/send-menu.ts, used by ShellSidebar and Sidebar); a menu of the owner's agents alone is unheaded and untagged (e8211d01). Evidence: thread-owner.test.ts 'for a LAN viewer, one press sends to the owner's newest live agent...', '...only other people's agents live, Send opens the menu', '...unheaded and untagged'; send-target.test.ts 'sendsFor'; e2e lan-send.spec.ts (a real LAN address, 0.0.0.0 bind) and agent-strip.spec.ts pass. Chromium at the LAN address, single owner: 'Send to claude', no caret, 'Send 2 unsent to claude', one press reads 'sent to claude'; with Sam connected: 'Send to claude', caret menu 'Alex's agents' then 'Sam's agents'.","supersedes":"2abc0c544ce6da85d3a58fc62a3b8394a111e7c194a223b28dc411e9c8db3307","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/view/publisher.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T03:13:17.317230Z","id":"9afd4bcf983ecb5cbe9c554a824dc3e48eb6d01cecc57a7b37a117cdcc88c369","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:07908a6b","summary":"Artifacts carry owner_name (crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs with_owner; an additive §19 key in tests/golden_single_owner.rs); the byline, the gallery card and the sidebar's fallback Send label read it. Roster and People-panel tokens are the name's initials ('sn'), titles 'sam-notes · Sam'; the inbox Agent filter lists agents by name and harnesses as 'All claude agents'. Evidence: publisher.test.ts, api_sessions publish_with_session_header_attributes_owner_and_versions / publish_without_header_has_no_owner, golden_single_owner::the_golden_differs_only_as_section_19_lists pass; Chromium: roster tokens ['sn','cl'] titled ['sam-notes · Sam','claude'], filter ['Any agent','All claude agents','claude'].","supersedes":"26259f1eb68709afb1695dd9f23fe8520b96f65b4c413d15706122e0c6c65229","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/view/artifact-controller.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T08:17:07.648351Z","id":"483a5418905be95c84697af37d3d803f00cdd1c68b867a65d8d095eacbffa2b7","body":{"detail":"Any query on a browser's shell URL now follows every page change, version link, the Latest link and copyLink: for example the inbox's /a/<aid>?thread=<tid> (crates/clax-server/src/inbox.rs:90), which nothing reads, sticks to every later URL and shared link. Line 714 (openPage) does the same.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":400},"end":{"line":402},"content_hash":"e8201d6adb3662a32030e0e48974f0db8215a485feaa840ee1345d8f7c498961"},"suggested_fix":"Carry only app=1 (e.g. a helper returning '?app=1' in app mode, else '').","summary":"here() and openPage keep the whole query, not just app=1","tags":["review","app-mode","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/view/artifact-controller.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T09:47:44.066416Z","id":"0d16c9722b024eb3f34ffec49a0aeb9bb4db6abb214cc908541749c09dbe67d3","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:130e2614","summary":"Fixed: here() and openPage carry only appQuery(location.search) ('?app=1' or ''); artifact-controller.test.ts 'carries app=1 in its URLs and no other query' and host.test.ts 'carries only app=1 from page to page, not the rest of the query' pass","supersedes":"483a5418905be95c84697af37d3d803f00cdd1c68b867a65d8d095eacbffa2b7","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/view/presence-reporter.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T13:56:47.117372Z","id":"af3fd3dd319ddd5961eb89d299881e7e73f874994da53a03a4dd71b3cbaf1fdb","body":{"detail":"Since 3fe7722b the stream takes app mode's visibility from the host (stream.ts visibility.hidden), but presence-reporter.ts (lines 26, 39, 55) still reads document.visibilityState, which the app's WKWebView reports as hidden from load on: the viewer's presence is 'away' for the whole session. web/shell/src/ui/card-sync.ts reads it too (gallery only).","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":55},"end":{"line":55},"content_hash":"5c4543f26dcd662c6134ee64c24ba8f2c9514cd384c57539dba578ef70a79318"},"suggested_fix":"Read visibility through one shared rule (stream.ts visibility.hidden, or a small module both import) and re-report on visibilityChanged.","summary":"Presence still reads the document's own visibility, so in the app the owner shows as away","tags":["review","app-mode","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/view/presence-reporter.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T14:00:15.096308Z","id":"720ecf8228951e4536c7c826c2fc149e8f921c3572b9884bc840f2e06d57b3e2","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:3c6753c7","summary":"Fixed in 3c6753c7: PresenceReporter reads visibility.hidden from web/shell/src/stream.ts (which app mode takes from the host) in report() and onInput. web/shell/src/view/presence-reporter.test.ts: 'follows the shared hidden rule, not the document's own visibility (app mode)' and 'reports away when the rule says hidden' (both failed before). cd web && npx vitest run -> '149 passed', '1548 passed'; npm run typecheck and lint exit 0; node web/scripts/bundle-size.mjs exit 0 (app host 3896). Not done: a re-report the moment the host changes visibility (the 30 s beat or the next input reports it).","supersedes":"af3fd3dd319ddd5961eb89d299881e7e73f874994da53a03a4dd71b3cbaf1fdb","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/view/after-paint.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T14:28:32.899659Z","id":"52616276f2004a98cec1277bdb0f8b5232a4b7370438314e224ed05d8dcaa1e0","body":{"detail":"node web/scripts/bundle-size.mjs at 11eaece3 against a clean build of 28134a83: artifact 64372 -> 64442, gallery 27736 -> 27830, comment part 11785 -> 11823, caps part 8691 -> 8745, app host 3896 -> 3919, extension composer 25648 -> 25791, extension overlay 18916 -> 18988; eager bridge unchanged at 5508. Over budget: artifact by 52, comment part by 2. web/perf/bundle-budget.json is unchanged.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":12},"end":{"line":20},"content_hash":"cce48f5560b56e857a196f21eb4d4a1dde5d0375c195c394b3744a56b7d5d83c"},"suggested_fix":"Raise artifact to 64448 and partComment to 11840 (measured, rounded up), or shrink the waits.","summary":"nextFrame grew the artifact bundle to 64442 gzip bytes (budget 64390) and the comment part to 11823 (budget 11821)","tags":["budget","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/view/after-paint.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T14:28:32.899750Z","id":"7cd9edc6e81c234d7ac861b77feffaff181bf367d4d13e37ea0fe455e5a3e17d","body":{"detail":"In the macOS app's WKWebView the shell and the page run no requestAnimationFrame callbacks (record 9e96bca7). Fixed to fall back to a timer: PromptDialog's Allow arming (whenShown: only while the app's host says shown, so a hidden browser tab still waits for a paint), Composer's status live region, the controller's address-bar fragment (artifact-controller.ts hashFrame), the bridge's hover outline (comment-mode.ts), a page's custom-anchor placements (bridge/src/caps/comments.ts), and anchor re-resolution on scroll/resize (bridge.ts, now a 50 ms timer). Already falling back: afterPaint (view start, reaction passes, presence, more menu, sidebar, gallery) and the room's flush (bridge/src/caps/room.ts). Not changed: Svelte transitions in ThreadCard.svelte and SelectionBar.svelte (the sidebar, hidden in app mode); the clip renderer (modern-screenshot) uses no animation frames. A new rAF wait a person can hit in app mode should use nextFrame (shell) or bridge/src/frame.ts.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":12},"end":{"line":20},"content_hash":"cce48f5560b56e857a196f21eb4d4a1dde5d0375c195c394b3744a56b7d5d83c"},"summary":"Animation-frame waits audited for app mode at 11eaece3: what waits on a frame and what falls back","tags":["app-mode","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/view/after-paint.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T14:29:23.135099Z","id":"571a2745d31fea5cfdf8bfb8312702d4d4b36ac4130af6384aaf9b90a1436240","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:411cc419","summary":"Budgets raised in 411cc419: artifact 64390 -> 64512, comment part 11821 -> 11904 (measurement plus 64, rounded up to 64). The growth is the animation-frame fallbacks of 11eaece3. node web/scripts/bundle-size.mjs after a fresh scripts/build-web.sh: 'artifact 64442', 'comment 11823', exit 0.","supersedes":"52616276f2004a98cec1277bdb0f8b5232a4b7370438314e224ed05d8dcaa1e0","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
